From c6952deb395ac89c407c84cb244a2820525b7965 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NexaFreight Rebuild <nexafreight-rebuild@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:10:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(map): rail shipments get a train marker, not a plane
 (day-12c)

Rail ROUTES rendered (purple dashed routes-rail layer) but every moving
RAIL marker fell into the FLIGHT bucket: the asset-type normalizer
mapped anything that was not VESSEL/SEA or TRUCK/ROAD to FLIGHT, so
trains flew with the plane glyph, green/orange click color and
'MARITIME (VESSEL)'-style mislabels.

Fix (frontend only; the backend interpolator already emits
asset_type=TransportMode -> 'RAIL'):
- normalizer gains TRAIN (rawType TRAIN/RAIL) before the FLIGHT fallback
- getAssetMarkerSvg + marker type unions widen to 'TRAIN' with a purple
  locomotive glyph (matches routes-rail #a855f7)
- marker-click mode map TRAIN -> RAIL with the rail color; popup labels
  gain 'RAIL FREIGHT (TRAIN)' (was 'MARITIME (VESSEL)' for trains)

Demo world has 34 RAIL legs (e.g. INCBE->INVNS), so the train shows up
immediately on the live map. Gates: tsc clean / 239 vitest.
---
 frontend/src/components/GlobeMap.tsx | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

